<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Home | Table Essence Point</title><meta name="description" content="Independent guidance for thoughtful table settings, seasonal menus, hosting rhythm and tableware care."><script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-0LY0HY7L01"></script><script>window.dataLayer=window.dataLayer||[];function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments)}gtag('consent','default',{analytics_storage:'denied',ad_storage:'denied',ad_user_data:'denied',ad_personalization:'denied'});gtag('js',new Date());gtag('config','G-0LY0HY7L01');</script><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/style.css"></head><body class="home"><header class="table-head"><a class="brand" href="index.php"><b>TEP</b><span>Table Essence Point</span></a><button class="menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav">Menu</button><nav id="main-nav"><a href="index.php">Home</a><a href="table-studio.html">Table Studio</a><a href="setting-index.html">Setting Index</a><a href="journal.html">Journal</a><a href="contact.html">Host Desk</a></nav><div class="service-note">LONDON / TABLE / GATHERING</div></header><main><section class="orbit-table" id="home-01"><div class="orbit-copy"><p class="eyebrow">01 / THE TABLE AS A MEETING POINT</p><h1>Set less.<br>Mean more.</h1><p>Table Essence Point is an independent guide to settings that make room for food, conversation and the natural pace of an evening.</p><a class="button" href="setting-index.html">Choose a setting</a></div><div class="hero-table"><img src="assets/images/core-hero.svg" alt="Top-down plan of a table arranged for six guests"><span class="seat s1">01</span><span class="seat s2">02</span><span class="seat s3">03</span><span class="seat s4">04</span></div><div class="orbit-caption">SIX PLACES / ONE CENTRE</div></section>
<section class="guest-coordinate" id="home-02"><header><p class="eyebrow">02 / GUEST COORDINATE</p><h2>Begin with people, then place the objects.</h2></header><div class="guest-grid"><article><b>01</b><h3>Reach</h3><p>Keep shared dishes and water within a natural movement.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h3>Sightline</h3><p>Let guests see one another across a low centre.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h3>Pause</h3><p>Leave enough open space for the table to breathe.</p></article><article><b>04</b><h3>Return</h3><p>Make clearing and resetting feel calm, not theatrical.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="palette-pantry" id="home-03"><div class="palette-copy"><p class="eyebrow">03 / PALETTE PANTRY</p><h2>Three colours can carry the whole table.</h2><p>Choose one quiet ground, one material tone and one seasonal accent. Repetition creates rhythm; small differences keep it human.</p><a href="journal-07.html">Build a three-colour table →</a></div><div class="colour-wells"><i style="--c:#f0e6d7"><span>Linen</span></i><i style="--c:#384c43"><span>Leaf</span></i><i style="--c:#d36a45"><span>Season</span></i></div></section>
<section class="service-clock" id="home-04"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / SERVICE CLOCK</p><h2>Let the evening move in five unhurried turns.</h2></div><img src="assets/images/core-service.svg" alt="Circular five-step service plan"><ol><li><b>18:30</b><span>Welcome</span></li><li><b>19:00</b><span>First plate</span></li><li><b>19:40</b><span>Main table</span></li><li><b>20:30</b><span>Clear</span></li><li><b>21:00</b><span>Close</span></li></ol></section>
<section class="vessel-cabinet" id="home-05"><header><p class="eyebrow">05 / VESSEL CABINET</p><h2>Give every piece one clear job.</h2></header><div class="cabinet"><article><i class="dish"></i><b>Plate</b><span>Frame the food</span></article><article><i class="glass"></i><b>Glass</b><span>Support the drink</span></article><article><i class="bowl"></i><b>Bowl</b><span>Hold warmth</span></article><article><i class="linen"></i><b>Linen</b><span>Soften the field</span></article></div></section>
<section class="menu-composition" id="home-06"><figure><img src="assets/images/core-studio.svg" alt="Material board with linen, colour and table plan samples"><figcaption>TABLE STUDIO / MATERIAL BOARD</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">06 / MENU COMPOSITION</p><h2>Plan flavour, texture and effort together.</h2><p>A useful menu balances crisp with soft, warm with fresh, and prepared-ahead elements with one or two moments that need attention.</p><a class="button dark" href="table-studio.html">Enter the studio</a></div></section>
<section class="conversation-field" id="home-07"><div class="field"><span>LISTEN</span><span>PASS</span><span>PAUSE</span><span>SHARE</span><i></i></div><div><p class="eyebrow">07 / CONVERSATION FIELD</p><h2>The centre should connect, not divide.</h2><p>Keep flowers, candles and serving pieces below the natural sightline. A centrepiece succeeds when it supports the gathering without asking to become the subject.</p><a href="journal-08.html">Design a low centrepiece →</a></div></section>
<section class="journal-servings" id="home-08"><header><p class="eyebrow">08 / RECENT SERVINGS</p><h2>Practical notes for a thoughtful table.</h2></header><div><a href="journal-01.html"><b>01</b><span>Scaling the table for the guest count</span><small>READ</small></a><a href="journal-03.html"><b>03</b><span>Setting candle height and light</span><small>READ</small></a><a href="journal-09.html"><b>09</b><span>Pacing a menu across the evening</span><small>READ</small></a></div></section>
<section class="final-toast" id="home-09"><div class="toast-mark">TEP</div><div><p class="eyebrow">09 / THE NEXT GATHERING</p><h2>Make the table generous, not crowded.</h2><p>Start with the people, choose what earns its place, and let the evening carry the rest.</p></div><a class="button light" href="journal.html">Read all twelve notes</a></section></main><footer><div><h3>Explore</h3><a href="table-studio.html">Table Studio</a><a href="setting-index.html">Setting Index</a><a href="journal.html">Serving Journal</a></div><div><h3>Contact</h3><p class="one-line">3638 Westbourne Grove, London, UK, W2 5SH, GB</p><a class="one-line" href="tel:+12125559857">+1 2125559857</a><a class="one-line" href="mailto:hello@tableessencepoint.com">hello@tableessencepoint.com</a></div><div><h3>Policies</h3><a href="privacy.html">Privacy</a><a href="terms.html">Terms</a><a href="refund.html">Refund</a><a href="shipping.html">Shipping</a></div></footer><aside class="consent"><p>Optional analytics helps us improve the serving journal.</p><button data-consent="accept">Allow</button><button data-consent="decline">Decline</button></aside><script src="assets/app.js"></script></body></html>